public/original.html is that chapter as mirrored, together with the stylesheet,
the six figures and the favicons it loads. Three things were changed while
mirroring, and all three are said in the attribution on the page: the Plausible
analytics script was removed, the chapter's relative links were rewritten as
absolute links back to cpu.land so they still reach the original, and the
canonical link was pointed at this copy.
The chapter's Google Fonts links are left as they are, because this is a mirror
of someone else's page.

public/index.html is the same chapter with nema added: one manifest, one script
tag, five inline question anchors, one activities block and an attribution
paragraph at the top and the bottom. Nothing of the chapter's text or markup was
changed. public/compare.html shows the exact diff.

This copy, and the nema additions inside it, are published under the same MIT
licence, with the copyright notice above kept as the licence requires.
Attribution: Lexi Mattick, https://cpu.land/the-basics.

The point of the mirror is to show what a learning protocol adds to an article
that already exists, on a real article rather than a demo one. If Lexi Mattick
would rather we did not host this copy, we will take it down: write to the
address on https://nema.migarci2.dev.

The rest of the nema repository is under the licence in the repository root
LICENSE file. This file governs apps/cpu/public only.
